  "request": "Which classes inherit from ApiModel (auto_ontology/server/models.py) only indirectly, i.e. through at least one intermediate class of this repository, and do not name ApiModel directly in their class statement? An import alias of ApiModel (auto_ontology/server/responses.py imports it as _Payload) counts as naming ApiModel directly, and a subscripted base such as ListResponse[T] counts as its class. For each, give the class symbol ID and the length of the shortest inheritance chain to ApiModel (2 when the parent class directly subclasses ApiModel).\n\nRequested output columns: class_symbol_id (string), depth (integer).",
  "explanation": "The query uses a recursive CTE to traverse the class inheritance graph. The base case identifies classes that directly subclass ApiModel and assigns them depth 2 (as specified). The recursive step finds classes whose parent class was already discovered, incrementing the depth. Finally, we select the minimum depth for each class symbol, which gives the shortest inheritance chain length to ApiModel.",
  "sql": "WITH RECURSIVE inheritance_tree AS (\n  -- Base case: classes that directly subclass ApiModel\n  SELECT s.symbol_id AS class_symbol_id, 2 AS depth\n  FROM code.symbols s\n  JOIN code.class_bases cb ON s.symbol_id = cb.class_symbol_id\n  WHERE cb.base_name = 'ApiModel'\n\n  UNION ALL\n\n  -- Recursive step: find classes that subclass the classes found so far\n  SELECT s.symbol_id, it.depth + 1\n  FROM code.symbols s\n  JOIN code.class_bases cb ON s.symbol_id = cb.class_symbol_id\n  JOIN inheritance_tree it ON cb.base_name = it.class_symbol_id\n  WHERE it.depth < 5  -- safety limit to prevent runaway recursion\n)\nSELECT class_symbol_id, MIN(depth) AS depth\nFROM inheritance_tree\nGROUP BY class_symbol_id\nORDER BY depth, class_symbol_id;",
